PACKET_SHA=b12b8887098e9b957bf17801266b83f1594aaefe4407a1ba058ae22319dc277f
GATE=PREREG_SOUND_WITH_REPAIRS
LEAK=content-level only: §1(ii)'s "derived, standard or measured inputs only, or a chosen, fitted, imported or undeclared one?" plus the co-primary rests_on tally imply the lane expects some claims to rest on chosen/fitted/imported/undeclared inputs, and the Planck-2018 STANDARD table implies a cosmology corpus; no direction, magnitude, comparison target, or preferred per-claim outcome is inferable.
CONSEQUENCE_VISIBLE=NO

STEP 1 — answered from the packet ALONE, before the master was opened.

Q5 (asked and answered before Q3): CAN I TELL, FROM THE PACKET ALONE, THAT ANY OUTCOME IS MORE
CONSEQUENTIAL THAN ANY OTHER? No. No sentence does. The packet's only consequence-adjacent
sentences are procedural stops ("stops the study", "The census does not proceed", "No tally is
filed", "do not adopt the passing seat's result") and one filing label ("INCONCLUSIVE, and it
takes precedence over CENSUS_COMPLETE") — these say what gets filed, never what anything is
worth to anyone. The one sentence that speaks to consequence at all denies it, packet §11:
"No tier, warrant token, standing or stamp moves." What a tier, warrant or stamp is, and whose,
is nowhere in the packet. CONSEQUENCE_VISIBLE=NO.

Q3: WHAT CAN I INFER ABOUT WHAT THE LANE EXPECTS OR HOPES THE CENSUS WILL SHOW?
Adversarial reconstruction of the stake from the packet alone:
  (a) The corpus is cosmology. The C3 closed list is the Planck 2018 TT,TE,EE+lowE+lensing
      baseline plus CODATA constants; no other domain would carry that table. Content, not stake.
  (b) The lane's interest is provenance, co-primary with reproduction. §1 states "two questions
      from one pass: (i) does the paper's own number follow from the paper's own recipe applied
      to the inputs it states; and (ii) what does that number rest on — derived, standard or
      measured inputs only, or a chosen, fitted, imported or undeclared one?" The "only, or"
      phrasing erects a clean-versus-tainted dichotomy, and the packet builds heavy machinery for
      exactly the tainted pole: a script-computed rests_on field reported beside every verdict, a
      DISPUTED tally row, transitive root origins. A census designer builds that tally only if it
      expects some claims to land on chosen/fitted/imported/undeclared roots. That is an
      expectation about the census's product — a leak of interest, content-level.
  (c) Failure outcomes are anticipated as real: the wording of a negative is legislated in
      advance ("unreproduced from the stated inputs," not "error"), and a 120-second timeout has
      its own per-claim outcome. Any honest census legislates for failure; this is weak evidence
      of expectation, not of preference.
  (d) Scale expectation: §6 budgets ~1 + 2–3 seat-days, so the lane expects a modest corpus.
What I CANNOT infer: any expected direction or magnitude (no "we expect N%", no "more", no
"less"), any comparison model or named target, any preferred per-claim or study-level outcome,
and what any tally would mean for any hypothesis — the packet contains no hypothesis at all.

STEP 2 — the master, judged as written, operative sections 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 11. Section 3's
core definition is settled under option (c) by the principal's ruling; §10 was read as history and
binds nothing below; no gate files were sought; no file other than the two named was opened for
content (all artefact checks were digests, existence booleans, or execution of the pinned scripts
on synthetic inputs in a temp directory — the script sources were never read).

1. OUTCOME CLASSES (Q1 placed here).
Per-claim: six outcomes, exhaustive over the decision tree §2 actually walks: no stated procedure
(REPRO_NO_DERIVATION_STATED); a needed input unprinted with a named source that is not an
enumerable pinned text or does not machine-match at the cited line (REPRO_BLOCKED); a needed
input neither printed nor traced to any named source (REPRO_INPUT_ABSENT); attempt exceeds the
cap or the lane's machinery (REPRO_NOT_EVALUABLE); attempt completes (REPRO_EXACT /
REPRO_FAILED). Mutual exclusivity is enforced by the stated precedence
(REPRO_NO_DERIVATION_STATED > REPRO_BLOCKED > REPRO_INPUT_ABSENT > REPRO_NOT_EVALUABLE >
arithmetic group), and the precedence is load-bearing, not decorative: a claim with one BLOCKED
and one ABSENT input genuinely satisfies two definitions and the order files BLOCKED. I could not
construct a real claim that escapes all six or lands in two after precedence. Study-level: seven
classes with a total precedence (R3C2_NO_CLASS > CENSUS_CONTROL_SPLIT >
CENSUS_DENOMINATOR_DISPUTED > CENSUS_ORIGIN_DISPUTED > CENSUS_AUDIT_FAILED > CENSUS_PARTIAL >
CENSUS_COMPLETE). A real tally fitting two classes: every claim arithmetic-group (COMPLETE's
condition) plus a failed audit re-derivation (AUDIT_FAILED's) — precedence files
CENSUS_AUDIT_FAILED. INCONCLUSIVE is genuinely reachable and indeed fragile in the right
direction: one single blocked or absent input anywhere in the corpus files one non-arithmetic
outcome, and CENSUS_PARTIAL "takes precedence over CENSUS_COMPLETE" — the inconclusive pole
cannot be defined away.

Q1 (asked directly): DOES §3 UNDER OPTION (c) MAKE EVERY DECLARED OUTCOME REACHABLE AND KEEP THE
REPRODUCTION QUESTION DECIDABLE? YES, as written. Hardest cases traced:
  - Printed-but-chosen input ("we adopt β = 1/929.25", no citation): §2 step 3 files status
    PRINTED; C3's reason code files ORIG_CHOICE_STATED → origin CHOSEN; §3's admissibility rule
    ("every ledger record with status PRINTED or STANDARD") lets the arithmetic consume it; the
    claim files exactly one of REPRO_EXACT / REPRO_FAILED and the script computes exactly one
    rests_on (USES_CHOSEN). The old tension — admissibility gating making the chosen-input case
    unreachable — is gone because status, not origin, gates consumption.
  - Fitted parameter the paper states: PRINTED + ORIG_FIT_STATED → FITTED; consumed; one outcome,
    rests_on USES_FITTED.
  - Imported value printed with a citation ("H₀ = 67.4 (Planck 2018)"): the reason-code
    precedence makes ORIG_CITATION win ("a sentence that names an external source for the value
    is a citation whatever else it says") → IMPORTED; consumed; rests_on USES_IMPORTED.
  - Cited-but-unprinted value: decidable mechanically — machine-match at the named source's cited
    line in a pinned enumerable text → PRINTED/IMPORTED and the attempt proceeds; otherwise
    REPRO_BLOCKED. No judgement residue.
  - Stated precision: "13.8 Gyr" against a reproduced 13.797 rounds to the printed numeral at the
    printed precision → REPRO_EXACT, mechanically.
The two residual judgement points — whether a passage "asserts a numeral as a result of its own"
(§1) and which reason code a sentence supports (C3) — are not class defects: both are assigned
to two independent seats with disagreement stops (CENSUS_DENOMINATOR_DISPUTED /
CENSUS_ORIGIN_DISPUTED), and C6 re-classifies every origin from the sources. The four earlier
failures on this tension are answered by the option-(c) split: reachability no longer depends on
an origin filter, and decidability is carried by status plus machine-match.

2. CONTROLS (Q2 placed here).
Every control names an exact code and every code is three-valued: C0_REACHABILITY,
C1_DENOMINATOR_PRINTED, C2_INPUT_LEDGER, C3_NO_SUBSTITUTION, C4_SEAT_ISOLATION,
C4_PACKET_REDACTED, C5_HARNESS_PINNED, C5B_NO_CROSS_LANE, C6_AUDIT_SAMPLE, each
PASS|FAIL|NOT_RUN, with "Controls in an unreached limb are NOT_RUN, never passes." No control can
be passed by bare assertion: C1/C2/C3/C5 require printed commands, stdout and exit statuses of
the pinned script and interpreter; C0's artefact is the exhibition table authored and verified by
two independent seats with the lane owner reduced to a coverage check; C4/C5b are self-reported
path lists and the document says so at their true strength ("PASS means the printed list contains
no such row and makes no claim that the list is complete"); C3's one seat-authored element
(completeness of an input list against the paper's equation) is named as seat-authored and routed
to C6, not implied to be machine-checked.

Q2 (asked directly): IS THE PROVENANCE FIELD CHECKABLE RATHER THAN ASSERTED? YES, with a stated
floor. Test — a wrong-but-plausible origin: the paper's line reads "We take the present-day
Hubble constant to be H₀ = 67.4 km s⁻¹ Mpc⁻¹ from Planck (2018)." A seat files origin CHOSEN with
ORIG_CHOICE_STATED and crops its verbatim to "We take the present-day Hubble constant to be H₀ =
67.4 km s⁻¹ Mpc⁻¹", omitting the citation. The machine passes it: the cropped string IS a
substring of the cited line, and I verified by execution that validate checks substring
containment, not line coverage. What catches it: the second seat's independent classification
quoting the full sentence files IMPORTED; merge records origin_alt; compute prints rests_on as a
DISPUTED pair (verified by execution: "rests_on=['USES_CHOSEN', 'USES_FITTED'] ... DISPUTED"); C6
re-classifies every origin from the pinned sources with no sampling discount on the arithmetic
group. What never catches it: the machine, and — if every reader crops identically — no one; the
master states exactly that floor in C3 rather than implying it away. I also verified the pairing
is machine-enforced below the floor: ORIG_FIT_STATED filed with origin CHOSEN fails validate
("reason_code ORIG_FIT_STATED does not map to origin CHOSEN"), and a DERIVED record's roots are
computed through the whole chain (cycle, dangling id, and parentless DERIVED all exit 1).

3. CIRCULARITY.
The expectation cannot reach the evidence through any of the four named channels. Inclusion: the
§1 rule contains no pattern vocabulary (verified: the packet copy contains no hit on pattern,
shape, magnitude, hypothesis, comparison model, or any named model token), is applied by two
independent seats, and any surviving disagreement stops the study with the disputed candidates
listed — no unilateral inclusion. Exclusion: five mechanical kinds, a separate exclusion ledger
with file/line/numeral/kind, and C6 audits "the full candidate and exclusion ledgers against
every pinned source — completeness, not just outcomes", so a contrary claim cannot be quietly
excluded: quiet exclusion requires two blind seats to agree and then to survive a full audit.
Origin classification: seats are blind to what rests_on means for anything (STEP 1), reason codes
are citation-backed with an explicit precedence, disagreements are reported as DISPUTED pairs,
never reconciled away. Interpretation: fixed before the evidence exists (see 5). The STANDARD
list itself cannot steer provenance: §2 makes the STANDARD/PRINTED status routes
"outcome-identical", and rests_on is computed from origin, which comes from quoted evidence, not
from status.

4. THE BLIND.
Machine-asserted as claimed, and verified beyond the claim where execution could reach. The
packet on disk (sha256 b12b8887…, matching R3C2_SEAT_PACKET.sha256, which also covers the seat
brief) contains exactly sections 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 9, 11 — §0, §7, §8, §10 absent, no SEAT-REDACT
tag residue — and a word probe found zero forbidden-list survivors (pattern, refute, expectation,
consequential, invisible, favourable, unfavourable, stake, prior, tempting, warn, the lane
owner's and engines' and custodians' names, R3D, magnitude, shape, gate, hypothesis, CDM: all
absent). The packet header embeds the master hash 47c55a74…, which is the ACCESS_SHA above, so
the packet provably derives from the gated master. I did not re-run the builder: running it
rewrites the pinned packet, which is a dispatch act, not a gate act; its output's properties were
verified instead. C4 as described prevents what it claims to prevent — a hand-assembled or stale
packet cannot dispatch ("a packet whose digest does not match its pin is not dispatched"; the
assertion is fail-closed: "the packet is not written and C4_PACKET_REDACTED=FAIL") — and the
document states the mechanism's limits at their true strength and no stronger: the blind is
"procedural, not enforced by the filesystem", the seat's path list is self-reported detection,
the forbidden list "blocks the enumerated strings and does not establish that every
consequence-bearing word is gone", and "It cannot prove a seat has no prior exposure from
training or an earlier session — nothing available here can."

5. THE SEAL (§7).
The receipted relay binds what it claims, before the step it must precede. Receipt P (protocol
hash + commit id, acknowledged and timestamped by the external custodian) must exist before limb
A begins — so the interpretation mapping is fixed before any evidence exists. Receipt T (tally
hash + commit id) must exist before the protocol is opened — so the tally is fixed before the
interpretation is known; neither side can be rewritten to suit the other. Post-opening, the
custodian re-hashes and verifies all four values, the interpretation report must print both
receipts and the four verified values, and any missing receipt or mismatch files
CENSUS_AUDIT_FAILED — which §4's definition explicitly names ("or the receipt verification of
the seal fails"). The C6 seed rides the same receipt, so the audit frame is frozen by the same
custody event. Limits stated honestly: a local commit "is tamper evidence, not an external
custodian", and "It does not prove Tori had not already guessed the answer — nothing available
here could prove that. It bounds the record, not the mind."

6. FAIRNESS.
Every negative outcome is worded at the evidence, not the paper: REPRO_FAILED carries the
mandated wording "unreproduced from the stated inputs," not "error"; REPRO_BLOCKED's cause is
assigned to the census's own scope ("the census may not open or consume it");
REPRO_NO_DERIVATION_STATED and REPRO_INPUT_ABSENT state facts and name the passage or input;
REPRO_NOT_EVALUABLE names the lane's own limitation. No operative clause uses "error" for a
paper. One name asserts more than its definition:

F2 (COSMETIC). Quote: "- **`REPRO_EXACT`** — the paper's number follows, within its own stated
precision". Defect: the name asserts exact equality while the definition admits rounding to the
printed numeral at the printed precision — a reproduced 13.797 against a printed "13.8" files
REPRO_EXACT without being exactly equal. Marked COSMETIC: the definition, the precedence, and
"Report both numbers" fully determine what is filed and reported; the name changes no class
filed, no control's passability, no reachability, no conclusion and no tested value. Exact
replacement if the principal wants it: rename the class REPRO_WITHIN_STATED_PRECISION at every
occurrence (a class rename is a redefinition and is the principal's call; the master's own
history records the escalation, which binds nothing here).

7. STALL / EXECUTABILITY (Q4 placed here).
Stall: every stall path has a declared landing. Per-claim timeout/machinery → REPRO_NOT_EVALUABLE
with one repeat; enumeration disagreement → CENSUS_DENOMINATOR_DISPUTED after two reconciliations;
input-list disagreement after merge exit 1 → one reconciliation, then CENSUS_DENOMINATOR_DISPUTED;
origin disagreement → DISPUTED pairs, CENSUS_ORIGIN_DISPUTED above 10%; missing seed →
C6_AUDIT_SAMPLE=NOT_RUN and CENSUS_AUDIT_FAILED with the missing seed named; missing or
mismatching receipts → CENSUS_AUDIT_FAILED; control failure everywhere → R3C2_NO_CLASS; split →
CENSUS_CONTROL_SPLIT with "do not adopt the passing seat's result"; C0 failure before freeze →
the preregistration never freezes, fail-closed by design.

Q4 (asked directly): CAN ANYTHING THE DOCUMENT DESCRIBES NOT BE EXECUTED AS DELIVERED? One thing
can not (F1 below). Everything else named was executed or verified as follows — scripts run only
on synthetic inputs in a temp directory, sources never read:
  - Files said to exist: r3c2_ledger_tools.py (digest bb5f1fc5… = the pin in §3/C3),
    r3c2_timeout.py (fbb9bef7… = the pin in §9), R3C2_CORPUS_MANIFEST.md (300d4da1… = the pin in
    §2), r3c2_seat_packet/R3C2_SEAT_PACKET.md (b12b8887… = R3C2_SEAT_PACKET.sha256, which also
    covers SEAT_BRIEF.md), r3c2_build_seat_packet.py (exists; not run — it writes the pinned
    packet), /Users/duhokim/HermesOps/scripts/nm_referee_dispatch.sh (exists at the absolute path
    §9 states), R3C2_INTERPRETATION_PROTOCOL_20260904.md (exists; §7's receipt P gates limb A on
    its committed hash, so it cannot be silently absent when needed).
  - Harness: /usr/bin/python3 is 3.9.6; sympy 1.14.0 imports under it — C5's three live commands
    execute.
  - validate: PASS on a clean ledger; FAIL on a planted rests_on, planted origin_alt, a PRINTED
    value absent from the cited line, a verbatim that is not a substring, an ABSENT record
    carrying a value, a BLOCKED record carrying a value, an ORIG_SILENT record without
    origin_search, and a reason_code/origin mispairing. ABSENT and BLOCKED records with
    "value": null PASS.
  - compute: writes per-record root_origins and per-claim rests_on to the output ledger and
    prints them; exit 2 on a ledger arriving with rests_on set; exit 1 on a cycle, on a dangling
    derived_from id, and on a DERIVED record with no parents; on a merged ledger with origin_alt
    it prints rests_on as a pair marked DISPUTED.
  - merge: exit 1 when the input_id sets differ; adds origin_alt and origin_evidence_alt on an
    origin disagreement.
  - census: exit 0 with reconciled=YES when declared counts equal recomputed counts; exit 1
    naming the mismatch otherwise.
  - wrapper: a fast command exits 0 with command, stdout, stderr, exit status and elapsed
    printed; a 3-second sleep under a 1.0-second cap printed SYMBOLIC_TIMEOUT, exited 124, and
    measured 1.004 s on the monotonic clock.

F1 (REQUIRED — Q4, changes a control's passability). Quotes: "A script asserts that … each
`STANDARD` value is one of a closed list PRINTED LITERALLY BELOW" (C3); "`STANDARD` (a measured
constant **on C3's closed list — that list, verbatim, and no other value**)" (§2 step 3). Defect:
the printed list and the delivered membership test are not the same list on the symbol axis, and
the value encoding is nowhere specified. Executed against the pinned script (bb5f1fc5… = pin):
  (i) 9 of the 14 printed rows FAIL when filed verbatim with the table's own symbols and values —
    ħ=1.054571817e-34, H₀=67.36, σ₈=0.8111, τ=0.0544, Ω_m=0.3153, Ω_Λ=0.6847, Ω_b h²=0.02237,
    Ω_c h²=0.1200, age=13.797 — each returning "STANDARD value … not on the closed list"; each of
    those values PASSES under an ASCII alias that appears nowhere in the document or packet
    (hbar, H0, sigma8, tau, Omega_m, Omega_L, Omega_b_h2, Omega_c_h2, age_Gyr respectively).
  (ii) The ln(10¹⁰ A_s)=3.044 row passed under no key among 16 tried; I cannot confirm that row
    exists in the delivered list at all (the script's source was not read, per the gate's limits).
  (iii) Values must be the exact printed string: G and c PASS as "6.67430e-11"/"2.99792458e8"
    strings but FAIL as JSON numbers ("6.6743e-11", "299792458.0"), and Ω_c h²'s printed "0.1200"
    serializes as 0.12. The C3 schema declares no type for `value`.
  Consequence: a seat applying §2's commanded rule ("Where a value the paper prints is on the
  closed list verbatim, file STANDARD") with the table as printed fails C3 through no judgement
  of its own; two seats can both fail (→ R3C2_NO_CLASS) or split on transcription
  (→ CENSUS_CONTROL_SPLIT). Exact replacement: add a third column "ledger key" to the C3 table
  giving the machine key for every row (G, c, hbar, k_B, H0, Omega_m, Omega_L, Omega_b_h2,
  Omega_c_h2, n_s, sigma8, tau, <the ln(10¹⁰ A_s) row's key — confirm it exists in the list>,
  age_Gyr), and add to the C3 schema: "`value` of a STANDARD record is the exact string printed
  in the table's value column." If any row's value is absent from the script's list, add it and
  re-pin the script in the same commit; the pin in §3/C3 must equal the delivered file's digest.

Verdict basis: the design's classes, controls, circularity closure, blind, seal, fairness and
stall structure are sound as written, and Q1/Q2 are YES under the settled option-(c) definition;
F1 is a bounded document-versus-artefact mismatch repairable by printing keys (or re-keying and
re-pinning the script); F2 is cosmetic and the principal's.

